{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And behold, she is with child.</b> She made no effort to conceal the disgrace out of respect for you, as in the statement of Amram, whose memory is for blessing (Yevamot 35a): a woman who commits adultery turns over or relations with you so that she not conceive."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {0 "The Hebrew קָלוֹן לִכְבוֹדְךָ is read as 'disgrace for your honor'; the reference is to Yevamot 35a, where the context concerns a woman who cooperates in relations in a manner intended to avoid conception."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:51.044204386Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}